{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Root cause pinned to production state — see `irongrey-chubby-oxpecker` for the full evidence\n\nDirect inspection of the live binding store (`git show origin/tickets:.bridge_state/bindings.json`)\nshows the comment-ID dedup map is **empty**:\n\n```\nbindings entries:      2475\ncomment_ids ENTRIES:      0\n```\n\nZero entries after thousands of successfully posted comments. The PRIMARY dedup skip\n(`binding_store.is_comment_mapped(local_comment_key)`, `outbound_comments.py:411-415`) therefore\n**can never fire**, leaving only the SECONDARY body-equality test — which the code itself\ndescribes as a belt-and-suspenders guard for a lost map write. That test compares a locally\nfitted+normalized body against bodies that round-tripped through ADF/wiki conversion, so rich\ncomments never match and are re-posted every hour, forever. REB-1861's comments are the richest\nin the affected set (40 local, avg 3.6 KB, heavy markdown) and match at **1 of 40** — which is why\nit filled Jira's 5000-comment cap first and reds this workflow.\n\n**Ruled out:** the previously-fixed pagination route (bug `1f3d-cb66-d3fc-4356`,\n`florid-vigorous-urial`) is NOT regressed — `get_comments` correctly uses `--paginate`\n(`acli_cli_ops.py:583-600`) and the snapshot truncation guard is in place\n(`outbound_comments.py:322-346`). This is the same failure class arriving by a different route.\nIts cleanup task `bd80-0603-7d44-4d9f` is the established precedent for purging duplicates\nafterward.\n\nStill unconfirmed and deliberately not fixed from static reading: which of the four silent\nno-op guards in `_record_comment_id` (`dispatch_apply_phases.py:309-334`) leaves the map empty.\nThat requires instrumenting a live pass and is AC 1 on `irongrey-chubby-oxpecker`.\n\nNo code change made; awaiting the operator's decision on scope and on whether to pause the\nworkflow to stop the ~205 duplicate comments/pass."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787251828697258001,"uuid":"82b57e86-bf64-48b9-b90d-99e7d2363116"}